      "value": "probe_exec"
    },
    {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "description",
      "value": "[auto-routed: 代码实验走真实执行] 1) Derive the exact 1D NLSE ground-state soliton (sech, not sech²) via symbolic Math: use `symbolic_math_tool action=pde_classify`/`pde_separation` on iψ_t + (1/2)ψ_xx + |ψ|²ψ = 0 to confirm the integrable structure, then verify by direct Ansatz substitution that ψ(x,t)=A·sech(A(x−vt))·e^{i(vx+(A²−v²)t/2)} with A·w=1 is an exact solution; explicitly document why sech² is a KdV mismatch. 2) Set up a conservative finite-difference/SSFM pipeline: choose Δx, Δt, domain L (large enough that tails are < machine precision at boundaries), with transparent/absorbing or sufficiently far Dirichlet boundaries; perform a grid-convergence study (h-refinement) to confirm the formal order of accuracy before testing the hypothesis. 3) Evolve from t=0 to t=10, recording ψ(x,t) at t=0,2,5,10; compute L2 error against the exact analytic projection on the same grid, discrete energy (L2 norm/power) and momentum, and nonlinear-solver residual per step to verify ≤10 iterations suffice. 4) Report: L2(t=10), max relative energy drift, max relative momentum drift, convergence order, and residual history; flag whether the stated tolerances are met or whether the format/initial-condition specification must be revised."
    },
    {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "expected_prediction",
      "value": "With a correct sech initial condition (A·w=1) and a conservative/high-order scheme (e.g. SSFM or Crank–Nicolson with small Δt), L2 error at t=10 should reach <1e-6 under grid refinement, energy drift <1e-8 and momentum drift <1e-7; if sech² is used as stated, the initial data is not an NLSE soliton and will emit radiation/breathe, producing L2 error ≫1e-6 — the test will fail for the wrong reason unless the hypothesis is corrected to sech."
    },
